    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "High school and college students are lacking the productive strategies and mindset to regulate their emotions effectively. From scholarly literature, our learner study and play tests with the game we designed, we found that the problem lies in the way these students think and talk about emotions and how they are unaware of their regulation strategies. As a result, we have designed a board game that provides practice in telling stories involving emotions in a more productive manner, and practice in the mindfulness of self and surroundings that is required for the productive emotion regulation strategy, namely cognitive reappraisal. Through observations and interviews during play tests, we have found evidence of our learners developing the growth mindset toward emotion regulation within the context of our game. We have also detected signals that our learners transfer the strategies and the mindset they learned to their real lives, but this is yet to be studied systematically to confirm external validity of our learning outcomes.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
